# {{.Title}}

Created with `gortisan create`. Every file here belongs to this project: nothing
imports gortisan, and gortisan is not in `go.mod`. Change anything.

## Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
./gortisan run               # builds cmd/api, runs it, restarts on every change
                             # (or: go run ./cmd/api)
curl localhost:8080/ping     # {"ping":"pong"}
curl localhost:8080/health   # {"status":"pass","checks":{...}}

```


## Layout

```
cmd/api/main.go           builds every dependency in order and starts the HTTP service
internal/
  domain/                 the business — no HTTP, no Kafka
    user/                 one package per subject; group them when there are many (sales/order)
      user.go             the struct — the table
      errors.go           failures in business terms (ErrNotFound…)
      store.go            what the service needs from storage
      repository.go       implements the store; its table mapping is generated at the end
      service.go          the rules — what the API and workers call
  api/                    HTTP
    router.go             /ping, /health, and one line per API version
    v1/routes.go          every v1 endpoint
    v1/users/           handler.go, request.go (inputs), response.go (outputs)

  platform/               infrastructure — no business rules
    config/ server/ validate/ health/
{{- if .Postgres}}
    database/ database/orm/
{{- end}}
{{- if .Redis}}
    cache/
{{- end}}


  arch_test.go            fails `go test` when a layer imports the wrong way
{{- if .Postgres}}
migrations/               SQL migrations, *.up.sql / *.down.sql
{{- end}}
```

Dependencies point one way — `api` → `domain` → `platform` —
and `internal/arch_test.go` enforces it, including that `api/v2` never imports
`api/v1`.

## Rules

- **Dependencies are passed, not looked up.** Constructors take what they need;
  `cmd/api/main.go` wires them. No globals, no values hidden in `context.Context`.
- **The domain names its errors** (`user.ErrNotFound`); the handler decides the
  HTTP status. Any other error becomes a 500 and is logged.
- **Validation returns every error at once.** `var errs validate.Errors`, then
  `errs.Add(...)` / `errs.Check(ctx, field, rule)`, then `return errs.Err()`.
{{- if .Postgres}}
- **Transactions are explicit.** `database.InTx(ctx, db, func(tx pgx.Tx) error { ... })`
  and `repo.WithTx(tx)`.

## The database layer

A model is a struct marked `//gortisan:table <name>`; every field with a `db` tag
is a column (`db:"id,pk"` for the primary key, `db:"created_at,default"` for a
column the database fills). Its mapping is generated into the end of the
package's `repository.go`, between `// gortisan:table <Type> begin` and `end` —
by `make:model`, by `./gortisan run` on every save, or by `./gortisan generate`.
To add a column, add a field and a migration. Nothing reads the tags at run time.
{{- end}}

## Generate more

`./gortisan` (`gortisan.bat` or `.\gortisan.ps1` on Windows) runs the gortisan
version this project was created with, through `go run`. It is not a dependency:
no code imports it and `go.mod` does not list it.

```bash
./gortisan list                                   # every command and flag
{{- if .Postgres}}
./gortisan make:model user                        # internal/domain/user + a migration
./gortisan make:model sales/order                 # a grouped subject
{{- end}}
./gortisan make:service user                      # internal/domain/user/service.go
./gortisan make:handler v1/user/list              # internal/api/v1/users: handler + ListRequest + ListResponse
./gortisan make:handler v2/user/list              # a second API version
./gortisan make:enum user/status --members "active,blocked"
./gortisan make:validator user/mobile_free
./gortisan make:middleware request_id
./gortisan make:client payment
{{- if .Postgres}}
./gortisan make:migration add_index_to_users
{{- end}}
{{- if .Redis}}
./gortisan make:cache user/profile --type "*User"
{{- end}}

```
